### Run after implementing the TODOs. Copy the id returned by request 1 into @productId.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082/api/products
@productId = 1

### Complete example: expect 200 with total 37.50
POST http://localhost:8082/api/examples/order-previews
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":3,"unitPrice":12.50}

### Complete example: expect 400 with errors.quantity and errors.unitPrice
POST http://localhost:8082/api/examples/order-previews
Content-Type: application/json

{"quantity":0,"unitPrice":-1}

### 1. Create: expect 201, Location, response DTO
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Notebook","sku":"BOOK-101","price":12.50,"category":"Stationery"}

### 2. Duplicate SKU: expect 409
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Another notebook","sku":"book-101","price":15,"category":"Stationery"}

### 3. Invalid body: expect 400 with errors for name, sku, price, category
POST {{baseUrl}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"","sku":"bad sku","price":0,"category":""}

### 4. Filter: expect 200 and an array
GET {{baseUrl}}?category=stationery&minPrice=10&maxPrice=20

### 5. Invalid filter: expect 400
GET {{baseUrl}}?minPrice=20&maxPrice=10

### 6. Read one: expect 200 (change @productId if needed)
GET {{baseUrl}}/{{productId}}

### 7. Update: expect 200
PUT {{baseUrl}}/{{productId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name":"Large notebook","sku":"BOOK-101","price":18.75,"category":"Stationery"}

### 8. Delete: expect 204; repeat for 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/{{productId}}
